# A TotalRate rule whose reactant pattern can match one molecule in more
# than one way: C declares two components named s, and the pattern names
# one of them, so it lands on either.
#
# This is the shape where RM and NFsim disagree.  NFsim expands the rule
# into one reaction class per symmetry permutation and gives each the whole
# total rate, so it runs at 2x this rate law; RM takes the rate law as the
# whole propensity.  BioNetGen cannot settle it, having never implemented
# TotalRate for network simulations.  RM refuses the model.
#
# Measured NFsim event rates against kf on this pattern shape: 1.00x with
# one free site, 2.02x with two, 2.98x with three.
begin model
begin parameters
  kf 0.5
end parameters
begin molecule types
  C(s,s)
  D(t)
end molecule types
begin species
  C(s,s) 200
  D(t)   400
end species
begin observables
  Molecules Dfree D(t)
end observables
begin reaction rules
  C(s) + D(t) -> C(s!1).D(t!1)  kf TotalRate
end reaction rules
end model
begin actions
writeXML()
end actions
